    farming: "The farming proverb says 'From Cold Dew to Frost's Descent, hurry to dig the sweet potatoes': the north must finish lifting tubers and autumn vegetables before the frost. In the middle and lower Yangtze, single-crop late rice is harvested and rapeseed transplanted, following the maxim 'rapeseed at Cold Dew, wheat at Frost's Descent'. Late rice in South China is heading and flowering and must be protected from 'Cold Dew wind', which lowers the grain-setting rate. Sowing of winter wheat in the Northwest and North China enters its final stage, while fruit growers are busy picking apples, pears, and hawthorn.",
