    scienceNote: "Start of Winter is not the same as meteorological winter. By the criterion of a five-day running mean temperature stably below 10 °C, at Start of Winter usually only the area north of the Qinling-Huaihe line has entered winter; the middle and lower Yangtze must wait about another half month, and South China often does not arrive at winter until Minor Snow or Major Snow. Astronomical winter, meanwhile, begins only at the Winter Solstice. So 'Start of Winter' describes the broad trend of continuing decline in solar radiation; the actual warmth or cold of any given place is not synchronized with it.",
    tip: "Winter begins its storing; south of the Yangtze and Huai it is still deep autumn."
