    scienceNote: "The solar term 'Minor Snow' does not mean it will snow that day, still less that any snowfall will be light. It only indicates that cold-air activity is strengthening, that precipitation may begin falling as snow, and that the snow-covered area gradually expands. Snowfall requires water vapor in clouds to deposit into ice crystals at low temperature and grow heavy enough to fall; whether the snow accumulates further depends on ground temperature. So there are often years with no snow at Minor Snow — or even at Major Snow. Solar-term names and weather forecasts are two different vocabularies.",
